-- #1111 A-2.5 (#1092): the FALSE-REJECT cell — a VALID program that the
-- bare-name method table rejected.
--
-- `mth` is selected from `mscopea` ONLY (`mscopeb`'s `mth` is never brought into
-- scope; only the type `MIB` is), so this occurrence unambiguously means
-- `MIA.mth`, and `Blob` DOES implement `MIA`.  The program is well typed and must
-- print `A`.
--
-- Before #1092 was drained it did not: the cross-module method table is keyed by
-- the BARE method name and is last-write-wins, `mscopeb` is loaded after
-- `mscopea`, so the impl obligation for this occurrence was recorded against
-- `MIB` — an interface this file never names — and `check`/`run`/`build` all
-- rejected it with `No impl of MIB for Blob`.  Verified first-hand on the
-- pre-fix binary in that exact shape (the `falserej` cell of the unit's probe).
--
-- ⚠️ This is the `exit 1 → exit 0` direction, which is a severity INCREASE if it
-- is wrong.  Its mirrors — the same graph with the impl missing, which must STILL
-- be rejected, and a missing impl with no collision anywhere — are pinned as
-- `test/analyze_project_fixtures/1092_method_scope_named_b` and
-- `.../method_missing_impl_no_collision`.
import mscopea.{MIA, mth}
import mscopeb.{MIB}

data Blob = Blob

impl MIA Blob where
  mth _ = "A"

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (mth Blob)
